# Agents

- Agents reason and delegate. Tools execute. The orchestrator coordinates. The policy engine authorizes.
- AGENT ≠ TOOL. AGENT ≠ BROWSER. AGENT ≠ PERMISSION. AGENT ≠ ORCHESTRATOR.
- Browser Use is a tool/capability, not an agent. Hermes is an external runtime, not a specialist agent.
- Specialist agents: `cto-architect`, `research-intelligence`, `product-ux`, `principal-engineer`, `growth-analytics`.
- Every agent must conform to `agents/contracts/agent-definition.md`.
- Handoffs must use `agents/contracts/handoff.md`. A handoff is not a chat message.
- Do not implement agent or orchestration runtimes unless the current task authorizes it.
- Preserve architectural boundaries when adding files or behavior.
